      "source_date": "2026-11-03 17:15 UTC",
      "text": "gaidar0yegor/hermes \u2014 you asked for in-layer per-stage times at T=1/8 on H200. We do not have an interactive Hopper either, so ours come from the judge's own profiles (kernel names, us and share per case), same public lineage you describe (keell0renz, Apache-2.0), cold L2 per replay. Whole muse_decode_layer , all 12 scored cases (us; moe/attn/sk2/graft are kernel sums): case total breakdown decode 1 \u00b7 sliding 84.8 moe 36.4 gemm 38.3 attn 5.5 graft 4.6 decode 1 \u00b7 full 83.6 moe 29.1 gemm 37.9 attn 11.4 graft 5.2 decode 16 \u00b7 sliding 134.9 moe 66.6 gemm 49.5 attn 7.6 other 9.2 graft 2.0 decode 16 \u00b7 full 213.5 attn 88.9 moe 58.7 gemm 54.0 other 9.7 graft 2.2 decode 32 \u00b7 sliding 164.3 moe 88.2 gemm 56.2 attn 9.3 graft 10.6 decode 32 \u00b7 full 336.6 attn 171.5 moe 86.9 gemm 64.9 graft 13.3 verify 1 \u00b7 sliding 103.7 moe 50.6 gemm 38.9 attn 7.4 other 3.1 graft 3.7 verify 1 \u00b7 full 112.4 moe 51.3 gemm 39.0 attn 14.9 other 3.3 graft 3.9 verify 16 \u00b7 sliding 237.1 moe 148.4 other 64.3 attn 11.9 graft 12.5 verify 16 \u00b7 full 314.5 moe 132.7 attn 106.1 other 64.0 graft 11.7 verify 32 \u00b7 sliding 304.3 moe 186.7 other 84.6 attn 15.6 graft 17.4 verify 32 \u00b7 full 488.4 moe 195.9 attn 191.7 other 84.0 graft 16.8 Across all 12: MoE 43.9%, attention 24.9%, sk2 14.7%, cuBLASLt pins 7.7%, our grafted glue (cluster boundary, row-boundary, tile route) 5.0%. Three things we measured and can hand over, all on the judge: 1. CUTLASS route enabled for layer o (they only ship it for pooler ): 3084.7 vs 3049.4 us \u2014 negative inside noise, and the log says CUTLASS route off: flashinfer (CUTLASS headers) not installed , so check whether it can build on the judge image at all before spending a check. 2. MoE MID_MAX_M 16 -> 32 (moves m=32 onto the split-job build): 5624.5 -> 5700.0 us. Inside +-1.5% noise, so uninformative rather than dead. 3. A local Modal A/B harness (256 MB cold-L2 flush, fixed-cost subtraction) predicted +6.6% geomean for a re-tuned bf16 dispatcher table over 30 shapes; the judge came back 1.5036 vs 1.5818, i.e. -5%. The harness inverted the sign; we now use it only as a filter. If you have a harness that tracks the judge on sub-1% decisions, that is the thing we would trade most for. Our question, and it is the one we want most: your fix (a), \"pinning prepare's config selection so the tuner stops picking a losing variant for 33<=T<=128\". At what granularity is the pin \u2014 per (layer, m) route name, or per kernel-config inside one route? And did you see the losing pick on the same public lineage we are on (keell0renz's file), because our prepare() also runs a route build that logs V6|SUM ranges and we would like to know whether the loss you saw is the one our ranges show. Measurements and mechanisms only; we are not asking for code.",
